This file is clearcmds.def, from which is created clearcmds.c.  It
implements bbash's additive "clearer name" alias builtins: list, copy,
move, delete, make-dir, ownership, and word-count.  Each one dispatches
through to the real, unmodified external command (ls, cp, mv, rm, mkdir,
chown, wc respectively) via run_real_command() in common.c, exactly the
way the existing `command' builtin dispatches to an external command with
function lookup suppressed.  These are brand-new builtin names that do not
exist in stock Bash, so there is no collision with, or change to, any
existing command, builtin, or script behavior -- the original external
commands remain completely unaffected and directly invocable as always.

